%% threading-and-dispatch: how a background-thread setter reaches the
%% reconciler. RenderContext checks the captured UI thread id, posts via
%% UIDispatcher.TryEnqueue, the marshalled lambda re-enters the setter
%% on the UI thread, the change-echo suppressor guards round-trip events,
%% and the reconciler does the rest on the dispatcher.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant BG as Background task
    participant Set as setX(value)
    participant UI as UI dispatcher
    participant RC as RenderContext
    participant R as Reconciler
    BG->>Set: setSeconds(s =&gt; s + 1)
    Set->>Set: MarshalIfOffUIThread checks _uiThreadId
    Set->>UI: TryEnqueue(() =&gt; Setter(value))
    Note over UI: queued
    UI->>Set: invokes lambda on UI thread
    Set->>RC: write hook slot
    RC->>R: requestRerender()
    R->>R: reconcile + flush effects
